			<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg>
						</summary>
							<p>Not yet officially, but Meta is planning to roll out creator monetization tools, such as branded content support, bonus incentives, and possibly tipping features.</p>						
					</details>
		<p>Yes, Threads has officially launched its direct messaging (DM) feature globally for Android, iOS, and web platforms as of early July 2025.</p><p>Yes, Threads is actively developing and plans to roll out GIF sharing and group chat functionality in future updates. These are among the highly anticipated features.</p><p>No, a Threads spokesperson has confirmed that DMs on the platform do not currently support end-to-end encryption. While they are protected by Meta\'s privacy standards and security infrastructure, Meta could potentially access message content.</p><p>Yes. You can access Threads via a desktop browser at threads.net, though some features (like posting) may still be smoother in the mobile app.</p><p>Not yet officially, but Meta is planning to roll out creator monetization tools, such as branded content support, bonus incentives, and possibly tipping features.</p>',
