    'excerpt' => 'Google June 2025 core update has launched, marking the second major algorithm update of the year. June core update follows the March 2025 core update and reflects Google\'s ongoing...',
    'body' => '<p><a href="https://searchengineland.com/google-june-2025-core-update-rolling-out-now-457731">Google June 2025 core update has launched, marking the second major algorithm update of the year. </a></p><p>June core  update follows the March 2025 core update and reflects Google\'s ongoing efforts to refine its search ranking systems. As expected, the rollout will take up to three weeks to complete. The update aims to further improve the quality and relevance of search results by prioritizing genuinely helpful, authoritative, and user-first content across the web. Like all core updates, it is not focused on specific content types or violations, but instead represents a broad enhancement to how Google understands and evaluates information.</p>		
			<h2>What are Core updates?
</h2>		
		<p>Google regularly releases Core Updates to improve the quality and relevance of its search results by reevaluating how its algorithm assesses content across the web. These updates are not aimed at specific websites or SEO tactics but instead focus on enhancing the overall user experience by delivering more helpful, trustworthy, and authoritative information. </p><p>When a Core Update rolls out, it can cause noticeable changes in website rankings, but this shift does not indicate a penalty. Instead, it means that Google’s updated systems now consider other content to be more relevant or higher quality for certain queries than before.</p><p>Most importantly, a core update does not represent a penalty against any particular site; rather, a drop in rankings after an update indicates that other content is now being viewed as more relevant or higher quality by Google\'s updated systems.</p>		
			<h2>Decoding Google\'s 2024 Core Algorithm Changes</h2>		
		<p>In 2024,<a href="https://searchengineland.com/google-algorithm-updates-2024-449417#:~:text=over%20the%20year.-,Four%20Google%20core%20updates%20in%202024,we%20expected%20across%20this%20work.%E2%80%9D"> Google released four core updates: March, August, November, and December. The March update was described as the largest core update in history, impacting multiple core systems.</a> These updates are designed to improve the overall quality of search results by better identifying and rewarding high-quality content. While reducing the visibility of low-quality or unhelpful content.</p>		
													<img width="768" height="439" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2024-core-update-768x439.webp" alt="June 2025core update" />													
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M508.55 171.51L362.18 150.2 296.77 17.81C290.89 5.98 279.42 0 267.95 0c-11.4 0-22.79 5.9-28.69 17.81l-65.43 132.38-146.38 21.29c-26.25 3.8-36.77 36.09-17.74 54.59l105.89 103-25.06 145.48C86.98 495.33 103.57 512 122.15 512c4.93 0 10-1.17 14.87-3.75l130.95-68.68 130.94 68.7c4.86 2.55 9.92 3.71 14.83 3.71 18.6 0 35.22-16.61 31.66-37.4l-25.03-145.49 105.91-102.98c19.04-18.5 8.52-50.8-17.73-54.6zm-121.74 123.2l-18.12 17.62 4.28 24.88 19.52 113.45-102.13-53.59-22.38-11.74.03-317.19 51.03 103.29 11.18 22.63 25.01 3.64 114.23 16.63-82.65 80.38z"></path></svg>				
									<h3>
							2024 March core update:						
					</h3>
									<p>
						It was a significant one, affecting multiple core systems. Google stated it aimed to reduce low-quality, unoriginal content in search results, with a projected 40% reduction, and later reported a 45% reduction.<br>Started: March 5, 2024<br>
Completed: April 19, 2024. It surprisingly takes 45 lengthy days to establish					</p>
				<a href="https://techbound.in/google-core-update-august-2024-lets-dive-in/" target="_blank">
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M508.55 171.51L362.18 150.2 296.77 17.81C290.89 5.98 279.42 0 267.95 0c-11.4 0-22.79 5.9-28.69 17.81l-65.43 132.38-146.38 21.29c-26.25 3.8-36.77 36.09-17.74 54.59l105.89 103-25.06 145.48C86.98 495.33 103.57 512 122.15 512c4.93 0 10-1.17 14.87-3.75l130.95-68.68 130.94 68.7c4.86 2.55 9.92 3.71 14.83 3.71 18.6 0 35.22-16.61 31.66-37.4l-25.03-145.49 105.91-102.98c19.04-18.5 8.52-50.8-17.73-54.6zm-121.74 123.2l-18.12 17.62 4.28 24.88 19.52 113.45-102.13-53.59-22.38-11.74.03-317.19 51.03 103.29 11.18 22.63 25.01 3.64 114.23 16.63-82.65 80.38z"></path></svg>				</a>
									<h3>
						<a href="https://techbound.in/google-core-update-august-2024-lets-dive-in/" target="_blank">
							2024 August core update:						</a>
					</h3>
									<p>
						This update focused on promoting helpful and high-quality content while demoting low-value SEO content. It also aimed to recognize improvements that sites may have made.<br>
Started: August 15, 2024<br>
Completed: September 3, 2024 (19 days).					</p>
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M508.55 171.51L362.18 150.2 296.77 17.81C290.89 5.98 279.42 0 267.95 0c-11.4 0-22.79 5.9-28.69 17.81l-65.43 132.38-146.38 21.29c-26.25 3.8-36.77 36.09-17.74 54.59l105.89 103-25.06 145.48C86.98 495.33 103.57 512 122.15 512c4.93 0 10-1.17 14.87-3.75l130.95-68.68 130.94 68.7c4.86 2.55 9.92 3.71 14.83 3.71 18.6 0 35.22-16.61 31.66-37.4l-25.03-145.49 105.91-102.98c19.04-18.5 8.52-50.8-17.73-54.6zm-121.74 123.2l-18.12 17.62 4.28 24.88 19.52 113.45-102.13-53.59-22.38-11.74.03-317.19 51.03 103.29 11.18 22.63 25.01 3.64 114.23 16.63-82.65 80.38z"></path></svg>				
									<h3>
							2024 November core update:						
					</h3>
									<p>
						This was a normal core update. Google is continuing efforts to show more high-quality, relevant, and authoritative content. While it caused volatility, it generally felt less impactful than the March and August updates for many sites.<br>
Launched on: November 11, 2024<br>
Completed on: December 5, 2024( 24 days).					</p>
				<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M508.55 171.51L362.18 150.2 296.77 17.81C290.89 5.98 279.42 0 267.95 0c-11.4 0-22.79 5.9-28.69 17.81l-65.43 132.38-146.38 21.29c-26.25 3.8-36.77 36.09-17.74 54.59l105.89 103-25.06 145.48C86.98 495.33 103.57 512 122.15 512c4.93 0 10-1.17 14.87-3.75l130.95-68.68 130.94 68.7c4.86 2.55 9.92 3.71 14.83 3.71 18.6 0 35.22-16.61 31.66-37.4l-25.03-145.49 105.91-102.98c19.04-18.5 8.52-50.8-17.73-54.6zm-121.74 123.2l-18.12 17.62 4.28 24.88 19.52 113.45-102.13-53.59-22.38-11.74.03-317.19 51.03 103.29 11.18 22.63 25.01 3.64 114.23 16.63-82.65 80.38z"></path></svg>				
									<h3>
							2024 December core update:						
					</h3>
									<p>
						This update came quickly after the November update. Google explained it was due to the different core systems they are always improving. Suggesting it focused on a separate aspect of ranking algorithms. Despite its speed, it brought notable volatility.<br>
Launched on: December 12, 2024<br>
Completed on: December 18, 2024. Surprisingly, it\'s only taken 6 days.					</p>
			<h2>Impact of the 2024 core updates.</h2>		
		<p>In 2024, the core update which target low-quality and AI-generated content. <a href="https://www.searchenginejournal.com/googles-march-2024-core-update-impact-hundreds-of-websites-deindexed/510981/?utm_source=chatgpt.com">The recent analysis reveals that over 800 websites have been deindexed from Google search results in the early stage of the update.</a></p><p>After the launch of the 2024 March core update, Google\'s SEO community has been tracking the indexing status of 49345 websites. Which is associated with manual action against AI-generated spam. So, this finding sheds light on the sweeping impact of Google\'s latest initiative. By monitoring the 49345 websites, there are 837 websites that have been removed from the entire Google search index.</p><p>It is a significant loss of traffic and revenue for them. According to the analysis, 873 deindexed sites have 20.7 million organic visits per month before manual action. The impact of the March core caused the website a sudden loss of traffic, devastatingly impacting the website.</p><p>There is not only a loss to the website because of the core updates,</p><p>A website that thrives by focusing on originality, depth, and real audience needs gets indexed on Google search and gets more traffic. Kind to 10+ Various independent site owners reported gains during the same update. They shared it on the Reddit platform.</p><p>This core update emphasized human-first content, meaning high-quality, genuinely useful material rewarded visibility, while low-effort mass-produced content was demoted or removed.</p>		
			<h2>The March 2025 Core Update: Explained</h2>		
		<p>Google\'s first core update of 2025 was the March 2025 Core Update<b>.</b> This was a wide update to Google\'s ranking systems. Its primary goal was to continue refining how Google <a href="https://searchengineland.com/google-march-2025-core-update-rolling-out-now-453253">Examines content to deliver more helpful, relevant, and high-quality results to users.</a> It wasn\'t about targeting specific sites but rather a general re-evaluation of content across the web.</p><p>Rolling out on: March 13, 2025<br />Completed on: March 27, 2025<br />It took 14 days to fully deploy.</p><p><b>Key aspect of the March core update:</b></p><ul><li><b>Emphasis on E-E-A-T</b>: Google continued to heavily emphasize Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness. Websites and content that showed these qualities were generally favored.</li><li><b>AI Content Mitigation</b><b>:</b> Aimed to reduce the visibility of low-quality AI-generated content and content that primarily serves to manipulate search rankings rather than giving genuine value to users.</li><li><b>Focus on Content Quality:</b> The update emphasized content that is helpful, relevant, and trustworthy, rewarding websites that provide a positive user experience.</li><li><b>Interactive Media:</b> Websites were encouraged to include interactive media like videos and infographics to enhance user engagement and improve rankings.<p>It\'s important to remember that recovery from a core update can take time, sometimes not fully manifesting until the next core update. The focus should always be on creating high-quality, people-first content.</p></li></ul>		
			<h2>Google launched: June 2025 core updates.</h2>		
		<p>This is the second core update of 2025 and this update will take about 3 weeks to complete.</p><p>The June 2025 update is a wide change to Google\'s ranking systems, designed to improve the quality and relevance of search results. It\'s not targeted at specific types of content or violations, but rather a general refinement of how Google Audits content.</p><p><b>Expecting Key Focus Areas:</b></p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400">Prioritizing genuinely helpful, authoritative, and high-quality content.</li><li style="font-weight: 400">Reinforcing the importance of mobile optimization.</li><li style="font-weight: 400">Rewarding content that demonstrates strong E-E-A-T signals.</li><li style="font-weight: 400">Further integrating AI to understand content quality and relevance.</li><li style="font-weight: 400">Focusing on page load speeds, mobile optimization, and overall user experience.</li></ul><p><b>Rolling out details:</b></p><p>Started on: June 30, 2025<br />Completion on: June 21, 2025  (expected)</p>		
			<h2>June 2025 Core Update: Final Thoughts</h2>		
		<p>The June 2025 core update highlights Google\'s continued evolution toward a more intelligent and user-centric search experience. It emphasizes that long-term SEO success depends on creating genuinely valuable, trustworthy, and user-first content, adapting to the growing role of AI in search, and building a strong online presence that puts user needs first. For digital teams, this update serves as a renewed call to focus on quality content in an increasingly AI-driven and zero-click search environment.</p>',
