    'id' => 51736,
    'slug' => 'social-media-updates-2025-june-trends',
    'title' => 'What’s New on Social Media: June 2025 Updates to Boost Your Online Game',
    'category' => 'Social Media Marketing',
    'tags' => 'Social Media Marketing',
    'author' => 'TechBound Team',
    'author_designation' => 'Digital Marketing Team',
    'excerpt' => 'Social media updates never stop, and June 2025 brings a wave of cool new features to help you connect with your audience. Whether you’re a digital marketing agency, a study abroad...',
    'body' => '<p>Social media updates never stop, and June 2025 brings a wave of cool new features to help you connect with your audience. </p><p>Whether you’re a digital marketing agency, a study abroad institute, or a health influencer, these updates from June 3 to June 12, 2025, are packed with ways to grow your brand.</p><p> We’ll break them down in simple words, sharing practical ideas to make them work for you. Get ready for a friendly, helpful guide to the latest social media trends!</p>		
			<h3>Pinterest Makes Searches Smarter</h3>		
		<p><a href="https://newsroom.pinterest.com/news/the-2025-pinterest-summer-trend-report/">Pinterest</a> updated its search to better understand what users like by looking at their past searches and saved pins. </p><p>This helps your pins show up for people who are into your topic, making it easier to get noticed.</p><p>For TechBound Innovations, a shipping-focused digital marketing agency, this is a win. </p><p>They pin a colorful guide on “Green Shipping Ideas.” With the new search, it appears for users looking up “eco-friendly logistics” or saving green tips, driving 25% more clicks to their client’s website.</p><p> If you’re in shipping, try pinning something like “Cheap Shipping Tricks.” </p><p>It could reach logistics fans, boosting your site visits by 20%.</p>		
			<h4>Google’s AI Influencers Share Tips</h4>		
		<p>Google’s “<a href="https://www.socialmediatoday.com/news/google-tests-portraits-ai-generated-celebrity-bots/750002/">Portraits</a>” lets you talk to AI versions of real influencers.</p><p>A health influencer asks the AI @anushkasharma how to keep followers excited about fitness.</p><p> The bot suggests sharing personal wellness stories, so they post about their yoga journey, which gets 30% more likes and comments. </p><p>If you’re a wellness pro, you could ask the AI for ideas, then share a post about your health journey, seeing 25% more engagement from your fans.</p>		
			<h5>LinkedIn Makes Video Ads Pop </h5>		
		<p><a href="https://www.financialexpress.com/business/brandwagon-linkedin-bets-big-on-video-to-drive-b2b-sales-3868016/">LinkedIn’s video ads now work great on TVs and phones</a>, with “First Impression Ads” that show up before other ads. This helps businesses catch the eye of professionals.</p><p>TechBound Innovations creates a LinkedIn video ad for a shipping client’s new tracking tool. </p><p>Using First Impression Ads on TV, it plays first during a logistics webinar, reaching 4,000 pros and getting 35% more sign-ups for demos. </p><p>If you’re in shipping, an ad for a logistics app could reach 3,500 viewers at a trade event, sparking 30% more interest in your services.</p>		
			<h6>Snapchat’s New App Makes AR Fun</h6>		
		<p><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/technology/tech-news/snap-introduces-next-gen-specs-ar-glasses-snap-os-platform-what-s-new-125061100752_1.html">Snapchat’s Lens</a> Studio 5.10 app lets anyone create augmented reality (AR) lenses without coding. </p><p>With games and custom Bitmojis, it’s a great way to grab young users’ attention.</p><p>A health influencer builds an AR lens where users try virtual workout clothes and play a “jump rope” game to unlock a discount on their fitness app. </p><p>It spreads fast, driving 1,500 downloads in a week. If you’re in wellness, a lens with yoga gear and a stretching game could go viral with teens, bringing 1,200 visits to your site in days.</p>		
			<h2>YouTube Boosts Livestreams with Interactive Leaderboards </h2>		
		<p><a href="https://www.androidcentral.com/apps-software/youtube/youtube-is-testing-a-leaderboard-to-show-off-top-live-stream-fans">YouTube is enhancing livestreams with a new leaderboard feature</a>, launched , where fans earn points for sending stickers, gifts, or comments, making streams more engaging and fun.</p><p> Additionally, <a href="https://techbound.in/google-lens-youtube-shorts-integration/">YouTube Shorts now integrate Google Lens</a>, allowing viewers to identify products or places in videos, driving real-world connections. </p><p>For example, a shipping agency hosts a YouTube livestream on supply chain tips, with fans competing on the leaderboard via comments and stickers.</p><p> The top fan earns a shoutout, boosting gifts by 35% and growing the channel’s followers. </p><h6>The Google Lens Magic </h6><p>Meanwhile, a study abroad institute streams a campus tour Short; a viewer uses Google Lens to find the school, visits its website, and enrolls, creating tangible leads.</p><p> If you’re in logistics or education, hosting a livestream on industry trends or campus tours, enhanced by leaderboards and Google Lens, could significantly increase engagement, followers, and conversions.</p>		
			<h3>WhatsApp Status Adds Flair</h3>		
		<p>WhatsApp’s Status feature, like Stories, now lets you add music, photo collages, and stickers, making updates more eye-catching.</p>		
			<h3>LinkedIn Tracks Post Impact Better </h3>		
		<p>LinkedIn’s new analytics show how posts lead to profile views, new followers, or website clicks, helping you make content that works for your career goals.</p>		
			<h4>Threads Gives Links More Likes</h4>		
		<p>Threads is boosting link posts to reach more users, with options to add multiple links to your profile and track clicks. </p><p>But since Meta sometimes limits links, it’s smart to use other platforms too.</p>		
			<h2>Meta’s Ray-Ban Glasses Help More People</h2>		
		<p>Meta’s Ray-Ban AI glasses now work with the “Be My Eyes” app, letting vision-impaired users get help from volunteers through video calls, making the tech more useful.</p><p>A health influencer with vision challenges uses the glasses to read a nutrition label while shopping, with a volunteer’s help. </p><p>Sharing this story online builds trust with followers. If you’re in wellness, showing how you use this tech could make your audience feel closer to your brand.</p>		
			<h3>Instagram Sparks Creativity </h3>		
		<p><a href="https://www.hindustantimes.com/technology/instagram-will-finally-let-users-rearrange-profile-grid-all-details-101749794848666.html">Instagram lets you rearrange your profile grid for a fresh look</a>, share Spotify songs in Notes, and funds new creators through its “Drafts” project.</p><p> A campaign with artists like Tyler, The Creator inspires everyone to get creative.</p><p>A shipping agency updates their Instagram grid for a clean vibe, increasing profile visits by 10%.</p><p> A Spotify song in Notes starts chats with followers, and a “Drafts” pitch for a logistics video series gets 4,000 Reel views. </p><p>If you’re in logistics, a sharp grid and music in Notes could lift engagement, with funding ideas pushing your reach further.</p>		
			<h2>Why These Are Awesome Social Media Updates in 2025
</h2>		
		<p>These June 2025 changes show social media’s focus on getting personal, fun, and creator-friendly. </p><p>For agencies like TechBound Innovations, Pinterest’s search and LinkedIn’s ads hit niche markets. </p><p>Study abroad institutes can use Instagram’s stats and Threads’ links to grab leads. Health influencers shine with Snapchat’s AR and Google’s AI tips, growing their fanbase.</p><h5><b>How to Get Started:</b></h5><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Pin specific topics on Pinterest to reach the right crowd.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Use Instagram’s reports to find the best posting times.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Make Snapchat AR lenses for fun, shareable content.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Try Threads links but keep other traffic sources strong.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Run YouTube livestreams to build a lively community.</li></ul><p>Jump into these features, test what works, and watch your social media take off!</p>',
    'image' => 'https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Social-Media-Updates-2025.jpg',
    'published_at' => '2025-06-13 11:00:49',
    'active' => 1,
  ],
  [
    'id' => 51730,
    'slug' => 'zero-click-ai-video-seo-trends-2025',
    'title' => 'Zero-Click Searches in 2025: Navigating AI Search and Video SEO Challenges',
    'category' => 'Search Engine Optimization',
    'tags' => 'Search Engine Optimization',
    'author' => 'TechBound Team',
    'author_designation' => 'Digital Marketing Team',
    'excerpt' => 'The digital search landscape is rapidly evolving in 2025. Google continues to dominate, handling over 5 trillion searches in 2024, while AI tools like ChatGPT are emerging but...',
    'body' => '<p>The digital search landscape is rapidly evolving in 2025.</p><p><a href="https://www.searchpilot.com/resources/blog/search-isnt-dead-its-just-getting-smarter"> Google continues to dominate, handling over 5 trillion searches in 2024, while AI tools like ChatGPT are emerging but hold a mere 1% market share</a>.</p><p> A significant trend is the rise of "zero-click" searches, where answers are displayed directly on the search results page.</p><p>A Q1 2025 report from Datos and SparkToro indicates that 27.2% of U.S. searches and 26.1% of EU/UK searches are zero-click, an increase from 24.4% and 23.6% in 2024. </p><p>This offers quick answers for users but presents a challenge for SEO professionals striving for website visits. </p><p>Video SEO is also becoming a crucial strategy for online visibility. This article will explore these 2025 search trends in an accessible manner.</p>		
			<h2>A Look at Search in 2025
</h2>		
		<p>Imagine searching "best pizza recipe" and finding the full recipe on the Google results page—this is a zero-click search, and its prevalence is growing.</p><p> While AI tools like<a href="https://tymoo.ai/knowledge-base/ai-search/the-top-ai-search-engines-for-2025"> ChatGPT and Perplexity are attempting to compete, they remain minor players</a>. </p><p>Traditional search remains strong, with 10.55% usage in the U.S. and 10.25% in the EU/UK, compared to AI tools at 0.55% and 0.71%.</p><p><a href="https://www.statista.com/statistics/265825/number-of-searches-worldwide/"> YouTube, a Google subsidiary, is the most popular search destination, accounting for 14.3% of U.S. search clicks</a>.</p><p> Let\'s delve into the challenges facing SEO professionals and the increasing importance of video SEO.</p>		
			<h2>Challenges for SEO Professionals
</h2>		
		<p>SEO experts in 2025 are navigating significant shifts. The primary issues include:</p><h5><b>Zero-Click Searches Reduce Website Visits</b></h5><p>Direct answers on Google\'s results page lead to fewer website clicks. Click-through rates decreased to 40.3% in the U.S. and 43.5% in the EU/UK in Q1 2025.</p><h5><b>AI Searches Are Growing:</b></h5><p>AI tools provide direct answers, and Google\'s AI overviews are becoming more common, fundamentally changing search behavior.</p><h5><b>Content Must Suit Machines</b></h5><p>SEO now prioritizes content optimized for AI and search engines—clear, structured information—rather than solely for human readers.</p><h5><b>YouTube Is Key</b></h5><p>As a leading search platform, YouTube necessitates video content for effective online visibility.</p>		
			<h3>How SEO Professionals Can Adapt
</h3>		
		<p>To stay ahead, SEO experts can implement the following strategies:</p><h5><b>Target Search Page Features</b></h5><p>Craft concise, clear answers to common questions to appear in Google\'s featured snippets or knowledge panels (e.g., "What is X?" or "How to do Y?").</p><h5><b>Use Specific Keywords</b></h5><p>Focus on long-tail, detailed keywords such as "best vegan pizza recipe for beginners" to attract qualified clicks.</p><h5><b>Focus on Video SEO</b></h5><p>Create optimized YouTube videos with keyword-rich titles, descriptions, and tags, including links back to your website.</p><h5><b>Add Structured Data</b></h5><p>Utilize schema markup to help search engines understand your content and display it in rich results.</p><h5><b>Check Performance</b></h5><p>Monitor the impact of zero-clicks and AI on your website traffic using tools like Google Analytics and Search Console, adjusting strategies as needed.</p>		
			<h4>Why Video SEO Matters
</h4>		
		<p>Video SEO particularly <a href="https://techbound.in/youtube-seo-in-2024-all-you-need-to-know/">Youtube SEO</a> is a potent tool in 2025. YouTube transcends being merely a video platform; it functions as a search engine where users seek tutorials, reviews, and diverse information.</p><h5><b>Why Video SEO Is Important:</b></h5><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">YouTube is the top search destination, capturing 14.3% of U.S. Google search clicks.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Videos often appear in Google\'s special search results, enhancing visibility.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Users increasingly prefer video for quick, comprehensible answers, particularly for "how-to" content.</li></ul>		
			<h5>How to Do Video SEO:
</h5>		
		<ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Keywords:</b> Identify relevant keywords (e.g., "how to bake a cake") and incorporate them into your video title, description, and tags.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Title:</b> Keep it concise, under 100 characters (e.g., "Easy Cake Recipe in 10 Steps").</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Description:</b> Write 100–250 words with keywords and a link to your website (e.g., "Learn to bake a cake with this simple guide! Full recipe: [yourwebsite.com]").</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Thumbnail:</b> Design a bright, attention-grabbing image (1280x720px).</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Captions:</b> Add subtitles for accessibility and to assist search engines in indexing your content.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Engagement:</b> Encourage viewers to like, comment, and subscribe to boost rankings.</li></ul>		
			<h2>Benefits for Everyday Users
</h2>		
		<p>For the average user, 2025 offers enhanced search convenience.</p><p> Zero-click searches provide instant answers for information like weather or sports scores without the need to visit external websites. </p><p>AI tools like ChatGPT are useful for quick explanations or brainstorming, though they can sometimes produce errors.</p><p> Google\'s AI overviews are helpful, but it\'s advisable to verify information for critical topics such as health. YouTube is an excellent resource for learning new skills, </p>		
			<h3>Advice for Careful Users
</h3>		
		<p>For those who prioritize information verification, vigilance is key. AI overviews may contain inaccuracies or draw from unreliable sources. To ensure accuracy:</p><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Consult the sources cited within AI overviews and visit those websites.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Compare answers from different search engines like Google, Perplexity, or Bing..</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">For important topics, rely on trusted websites, particularly those ending in ".gov" or ".edu."</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Utilize search operators such as "site:.edu" to find reliable results.</li></ul>		
			<h2>Conclusion: Machines Are Growing, But People Are Still Needed
</h2>		
		<p>In 2025, the search landscape is a dynamic blend of human needs and machine capabilities. </p><p>Zero-click searches and AI tools streamline the user experience but present challenges for SEO professionals. </p><p>Optimizing content for algorithms is now a significant aspect of SEO, yet human creativity and judgment remain essential. </p><p>Video SEO, especially on YouTube, is a must for maintaining visibility. </p><p>While AI continues to expand, human discernment remains crucial. </p><p>Whether you\'re an SEO expert, a casual searcher, or a meticulous fact-checker, the search world is evolving, and staying informed is paramount.</p>',
