    'id' => 49886,
    'slug' => 'google-core-update-august-2024-lets-dive-in',
    'title' => 'Google Core Update August 2024: Let’s Dive In',
    'category' => 'Digital Marketing',
    'tags' => 'Digital Marketing',
    'author' => 'Kishor',
    'author_designation' => 'Founder & Lead Strategist',
    'excerpt' => 'Google makes several changes and additions in algorithms within a year. Google Core update August 2024 was released on 15th. The rollout may take up to a month to complete. After...',
    'body' => '<p>Google makes several changes and additions in algorithms within a year. Google Core update August 2024 was released on 15th. The rollout may take up to a month to complete.</p><p> After releasing the August update,  Google Search confirmed a ranking bug, which was solved on 20th August.</p><p>Core updates are mainly focused on helping viewers to ensure a reliable and genuine search result. This is not targeting specific sites or individuals, and it\'s for improving overall search results by ensuring high-quality sites.</p><p>This blog will provide additional information on how core updates operate and will offer suggestions for evaluating and enhancing your content.</p>		
			<h2>Google core update August 2024
</h2>		
															<img width="1185" height="529" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-01.png" alt="" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-01.png 1185w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-01-300x134.png 300w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-01-1024x457.png 1024w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-01-768x343.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1185px) 100vw, 1185px" />															
		<p>Google aims to protect <a href="https://www.semrush.com/blog/quality-content/">high-quality, useful content</a> and reduce low-value, SEO-focused material.</p><p> You should implement a content strategy that makes sustainable improvements rather than quick fixes to enhance site quality and SEO rankings.</p><p> For instance, to easily understand the core update, let\'s say you are looking for a place\'s greatest boutique. And years ago you prepared a list of boutiques for some events. You cannot estimate the best boutique as per the previous list. </p><p>Because the names on the most recent list or those added to the top-ranking spots may not match the list from the previous list. </p><p>Some of them may occupy prominent positions because of their good services and new facilities, while others may disappear from the list. </p><p>It is not only because they are bad, but also due to there being just other restaurants that make your top 20.</p><h3>Focal Point</h3><ul><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Released on August 15, 2024.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Google Search confirmed a<a href="https://searchengineland.com/google-search-ranking-bug-unrelated-to-the-core-update-445246"> ranking bug</a>, which was solved on the 20th </li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Most probably, the core update will roll out completely within the last week of August.</li><li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">The main point of Google Core Update August 2024 is to demote low-value SEO-focused websites and promote high-quality websites.</li></ul>		
															<img width="1024" height="482" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-02-1024x482.png" alt="" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-02-1024x482.png 1024w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-02-300x141.png 300w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-02-768x361.png 768w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Google-core-update-August-2024-02.png 1228w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" />															
		<h3>Impact Analysis</h3><p>If you feel the ranking position is dropping, then by using Google Search Console, analyse thoroughly, identify the issues, and rectify them wisely. Don’t panic, stay calm, and confirm the following:</p><h6>1. Rollout has finished or not:</h6><p> Check <a href="https://status.search.google.com/incidents/42XCLGtpuCZkzqe4dc6S">google search status dashboard</a> to confirm the current status of the update. Confirm the date in which the core updates completely roll out.</p>		
															<img width="512" height="217" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/3rd.png" alt="" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/3rd.png 512w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/3rd-300x127.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 512px) 100vw, 512px" />															
		<h6>2. Compare the previous report with the latest:</h6><p>Maintain a report prior to the core upgrades, compare with the  current report to identify any discrepancies or new issues. Collaborate with experts to analyse these differences, understand their causes, and develop solutions. </p><h6>3. Analyse ran<b>king position: </b></h6><p>If the ranking has only slightly changed, such as moving a few positions, it may not warrant immediate action; such minor fluctuations often stabilise over time with careful observation and minor adjustments.</p><h6>4. Compare result:</h6><p>However, if there is a significant drop in ranking, for instance, a fall from 1st place to 50th, it indicates a serious issue that needs urgent attention. In such cases, conduct a thorough analysis to identify the root causes of the dramatic decline. </p><p>Collaborate with experts to diagnose the problem, implement corrective measures swiftly, and monitor the results closely to restore and improve the system\'s performance.</p><h3>Look Before you leap</h3><ul><li aria-level="1"><h5>Make a thorough audit report and note any weaknesses.</h5></li></ul><p>Verify the date of rollout and examine the report subsequent to that date. If there is a significant shift in your website\'s score, conduct a detailed investigation and arrange for a comprehensive audit.</p><ul><li aria-level="1"><h5>Never make hasty corrections.</h5></li></ul><p>Never make hasty modifications, and don\'t get rid of information you discover isn\'t optimal for search engine optimization. Make adjustments to improve the quality of your material and turn it into an SEO-friendly format. Make use of material that will benefit your audience. The text ought to be readable and informative.</p><p>Additionally, seek professional guidance after deciding to remove pages from your website.</p><p>If you\'ve made changes, it might take some time to observe a difference in search results</p><h3>Google core update August 2024: Recovery Tips</h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Recognize Google updates. Determine how these improvements will impact the ranking of your website.</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Make sure the users can access informative stuff on the website. And emphasise readability to keep the user experience intact.</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Optimise the content with relevant keywords and undergo SEO best practices.</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Incorporate structured data to improve your content\'s understanding by search engines.</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Avoid duplicate pages, orphaned pages, and broken links to enhance site quality.</li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Use tools such as Google Analytics and Google Search console</li>
</ul><h3>Recap</h3><p>After being released on June 27, <a href="https://techbound.in/googles-june-spam-update-high-quality-content-2024/">Google\'s June 2024 spam updates </a>significantly altered the SEO environment.Its main goals were to take down websites that were breaking Google\'s spam policies and to eradicate different kinds of online spam, which has an impact on rankings. </p><h2>To sum up</h2><p>Avoid making rash decisions and instead focus on sustainable improvements to your content. As the update finishes rolling out, monitor any major changes in your site\'s rankings and approach them with careful analysis and expert support. </p><p>Reach out to <a href="https://techbound.in">Techbound Innovations Pvt Ltd</a>, an SEO firm in Trivandrum, Kerala, for professional guidance and help navigating these changes successfully. We\'re here to support your adaptation and success. <a href="https://techbound.in/contact/">Our team of experts</a> can assist you in maintaining your top spot in the search results.</p><p>Techbound has over 12 years of experience in this area. You can use our extensive expertise and experience to reduce risks, improve your website\'s search engine rankings, and successfully increase your online presence.</p>',
    'image' => 'https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Google-core-update-August-2024-Banner-Image.webp',
    'published_at' => '2024-08-24 11:24:22',
    'active' => 1,
  ],
