    'excerpt' => 'Google’s June 2024 spam update, rolled out on June 27, 2024, marks a substantial change in the SEO landscape. This update strengthens Google’s focus on providing content helpful...',
    'body' => 'Google’s June 2024 spam update, rolled out on June 27, 2024, marks a substantial change in the SEO landscape.

This update strengthens Google’s focus on providing content helpful for the users and targets Websites, which violates Google\'s spam policies.

They are now prioritising high-quality, user-centric content and devaluing manipulative SEO tactics.

Content creators and digital marketers are now required to deeply understand the update’s implications and be willing to formulate strategies to keep up with the flow.
<h2>Exposing Google\'s Thought Process</h2>
Although Google doesn\'t reveal the specifics of its algorithm, its actions do.

<a href="https://techbound.in/google-sge-impact-is-seo-fading/">The Search Generative Experience (SGE) is one of the recent upgrades that has digital professionals in a panic.</a>

By placing summaries right in search results, SGE sabotages SEO efforts and may even move organic results down the page.

In a similar vein, it\'s anticipated that Gemini, Google\'s remarkable AI chatbot, would surpass all other chatbots in use.

And the march update directly targets two major problems in the online world: low-quality content and misleading SEO tactics.

Google optimises the user experience through these advances, eliminating various forms of web spam and producing high-quality content to better serve searchers.
<h2>Focal Points of Google’s June Spam updates</h2>
<img width="1019" height="584" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Googles-June-2024-spam-update.png" alt="Focal Points" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Googles-June-2024-spam-update.png 1019w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Googles-June-2024-spam-update-300x172.png 300w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Googles-June-2024-spam-update-768x440.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1019px) 100vw, 1019px">
<ul>
 	<li>Rolled out on June 27, 2024</li>
 	<li>Target the websites violating Google\'s spam policies</li>
 	<li>Eliminate various forms of web spam and it affects the ranking.</li>
</ul>
