    'excerpt' => 'Table of Contents Have you ever found yourself in those moments of curiosity, wondering about the actor in a movie or seeking the recipe for the perfect cheesecake? When these...',
    'body' => '<h4>
				Table of Contents</h4>
<svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M207.029 381.476L12.686 187.132c-9.373-9.373-9.373-24.569 0-33.941l22.667-22.667c9.357-9.357 24.522-9.375 33.901-.04L224 284.505l154.745-154.021c9.379-9.335 24.544-9.317 33.901.04l22.667 22.667c9.373 9.373 9.373 24.569 0 33.941L240.971 381.476c-9.373 9.372-24.569 9.372-33.942 0z"></path></svg>
<svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M240.971 130.524l194.343 194.343c9.373 9.373 9.373 24.569 0 33.941l-22.667 22.667c-9.357 9.357-24.522 9.375-33.901.04L224 227.495 69.255 381.516c-9.379 9.335-24.544 9.317-33.901-.04l-22.667-22.667c-9.373-9.373-9.373-24.569 0-33.941L207.03 130.525c9.372-9.373 24.568-9.373 33.941-.001z"></path></svg>
<svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M500 975V858C696 858 858 696 858 500S696 142 500 142 142 304 142 500H25C25 237 238 25 500 25S975 237 975 500 763 975 500 975Z"></path></svg>

Have you ever found yourself in those moments of curiosity, wondering about the actor in a movie or seeking the recipe for the perfect cheesecake? When these questions arise, there\'s a reflexive response that\'s become universal: we turn to <b>Google.</b>

<a href="https://www.google.com/" data-wplink-edit="true">Google</a> isn\'t just your average search engine; it\'s a tech powerhouse that transformed the way we explore information. On this special day, Google invites us to walk down memory lane, reminiscing about the incredible journey that brought us here today.&nbsp;

It\'s a testament to the relentless pursuit of knowledge and innovation that continues to define Google.

<img width="569" height="1024" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_152836-569x1024.jpg" alt="Google\'s 25th birthday" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_152836-569x1024.jpg 569w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_152836-167x300.jpg 167w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_152836-768x1382.jpg 768w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_152836-853x1536.jpg 853w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_152836.jpg 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 569px) 100vw, 569px">
<h2>Twitter Celebrates Google\'s 25th Birthday</h2>
As Google celebrates its 25th birthday, the Twittersphere is buzzing with warm wishes and fond memories. Users from around the world are sharing their stories of how Google has impacted their lives and transformed the way they access information.

<img width="707" height="1024" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162812-707x1024.jpg" alt="Twitter Celebrates Google\'s 25th Birthday" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162812-707x1024.jpg 707w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162812-207x300.jpg 207w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162812-768x1113.jpg 768w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162812-1060x1536.jpg 1060w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162812.jpg 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 707px) 100vw, 707px">
<img width="837" height="1024" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162829-1-837x1024.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162829-1-837x1024.jpg 837w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162829-1-245x300.jpg 245w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162829-1-768x940.jpg 768w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_20230927_162829-1.jpg 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 837px) 100vw, 837px">

As Google celebrates its <a href="https://www.google.com/doodles/googles-25th-birthday">25th birthday with a dazzling animated doodle on its homepage</a>, it\'s the perfect time to reflect on the story of innovation and ambition that led to its global dominance. Let\'s also take a walk down memory lane.

This is a tale of two graduate students, a modest dorm room, and a revolutionary idea that transformed the world as we knew it.
<h2>The Birth of Google</h2>
Our story begins in 1996 when Larry Page and Sergey Brin, two computer science graduate students at Stanford University, embarked on a mission to organize the ever-expanding World Wide Web.&nbsp;

At the time, the internet was a chaotic mess of unindexed web pages, making it challenging to find information quickly and efficiently.

<img width="678" height="452" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/images-7.jpeg" alt="larry page and sergey brin" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/images-7.jpeg 678w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/images-7-300x200.jpeg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 678px) 100vw, 678px">

Page and Brin developed a revolutionary algorithm called PageRank, which assessed the importance of web pages by analyzing their backlinks. This breakthrough allowed them to create a search engine that could deliver more relevant search results than ever before.&nbsp;

Initially, their project was named "Backrub," reflecting the focus on backlinks.
<h2>The Name Change</h2>
In 1997, the duo decided to change the name from Backrub to something more fitting. After brainstorming and considering various options, they settled on "Google," a play on the mathematical term <b><i>"</i></b><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Googol"><b><i>googol</i></b></a><b><i>," </i></b>which represents the number 1 followed by 100 zeros.&nbsp;

This name choice reflected their mission to organize an almost impossibly vast amount of information on the internet.
<h2>Google Inc. is Born</h2>
As the search engine gained popularity on Stanford\'s campus and beyond, Page and Brin realized its immense potential. In 1998, they founded Google Inc. in a garage belonging to a friend.&nbsp;

This marked the official beginning of Google as a company.
<h2>Initial Growth</h2>
Google\'s growth was rapid and relentless. In 1999, it secured its first significant round of funding, raising $25 million from venture capitalists. This funding allowed them to invest in infrastructure and expand their team.&nbsp;

The same year, Google moved its headquarters to a new location in Mountain View, California.
<h2>Going Public</h2>
One of the most significant milestones in Google\'s history was its initial public offering (IPO) on August 19, 2004. The company went public at a price of $85 per share, raising $1.67 billion in the process.&nbsp;

This move made Larry Page and Sergey Brin billionaires and solidified Google\'s position as a tech giant.
<h2>Diversification and Innovation</h2>
Google\'s mission has always been to <b><i>"organize the world\'s information and make it universally accessible and useful."</i></b> Over the years, the company expanded its services far beyond its original search engine.&nbsp;

Here are some of the key milestones in Google\'s diversification and innovation:
<ul>
 	<li><b>Gmail (2004):</b> Google launched its <a href="https://techbound.in/5-email-marketing-mistakes-to-avoid-in-2023-how-to-fix-them/">email service</a>, Gmail, on 1 April 2004 which quickly gained popularity due to its large storage capacity and innovative features.</li>
 	<li><b>Google Maps (2005):&nbsp;</b>The introduction of Google Maps on Feb 8, 2005 revolutionized navigation and location-based services.</li>
 	<li><b>Android (2005):&nbsp;</b>Google acquired Android Inc., in September 2008 laying the foundation for the world\'s most popular mobile operating system, Android.</li>
 	<li><b>Google Chrome (2008)</b>: The release of the Chrome web browser challenged the dominance of Internet Explorer and Firefox.</li>
 	<li><b>Google Drive (2012)</b>: Google\'s cloud storage service provided users with a seamless way to store and share files online.</li>
 	<li>&nbsp;<b>Google Assistant (2016)</b>: The development of AI-powered virtual assistants marked Google\'s foray into the world of artificial intelligence.</li>
 	<li><b>Alphabet Inc. (2015)</b>: Google restructured itself into Alphabet Inc., a conglomerate overseeing various subsidiaries, including Google, Waymo (self-driving cars), and Verily (life sciences).</li>
</ul>
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
Google\'s 25th birthday is a celebration of not just a search engine but a global phenomenon that has shaped the way we connect with information and each other.&nbsp;

From a modest dorm room project to a tech powerhouse, Google\'s journey has been nothing short of extraordinary.&nbsp;

As we wish Google a happy 25th birthday, we also celebrate the spirit of curiosity, innovation, and the endless pursuit of knowledge that it embodies.&nbsp;

<b>Cheers to another 25 years of exploration and discovery with Google!</b>',
