    'slug' => '5-email-marketing-mistakes-to-avoid-in-2023-how-to-fix-them',
    'title' => '5 Email Marketing Mistakes to Avoid in 2023 & How to Fix Them',
    'category' => 'Digital Marketing',
    'tags' => 'Digital Marketing',
    'author' => 'TechBound Team',
    'author_designation' => 'Digital Marketing Team',
    'excerpt' => 'Let me ask you this. When was the last time you opened your email and how many promotional emails you opened?. According to Mailchimp , the average open rate for emails across all...',
    'body' => '<p>Let me ask you this. When was the last time you opened your email and how many promotional emails you opened?. <a href="https://mailchimp.com/resources/email-marketing-benchmarks/">According to Mailchimp</a>, the average open rate for emails across all the industries analysed was 21.33%. So what is happening to the rest 78.67% mails. Is there any silver lining that is preventing those emails from falling to the open list. This might be because of the following Email Marketing Mistakes which nobody dares to share with you, </p>		
			<h1>Email Marketing Mistakes</h1>		
		<h2><strong>Unclear objective</strong></h2><ul><li>A goal without a plan is just a wish. I know you might have heard this multiple times. Email Marketing is not an exception. What normally Email marketers do is doing their routine tasks of creating and sending emails, but fails to include clear calls to action. This is where it is backfired. Selling too hard leads to audience unsubscribe from your newsletter and offer and even land you in spam list.</li><li>So decide what you want the recipient to do. Go straight with calls to action. Whether you want them to subscribe to your news letter or to buy your product, make it clear.</li></ul><h2><strong>Promoting Multiple Products</strong></h2><ul><li>Warren Buffet once said not to test the depth of a river with both feet. He was referring about taking risks in traditional marketing. It is also true in <a href="https://techbound.in/">digital marketing</a>. In reality, promoting multiple products in a single Email is not a risk worth taking. It will overwhelm and confuse email recipients and will not serve either of the purpose.</li><li><a href="https://blog.marketo.com/2018/02/email-subject-line-length-works-best.html">Marketo found</a> that Email subject lines with 41 characters across seven words the best approach. This is easier said than done. You can at least aim to make it under 60 characters which will help you stand out in someone’s inbox. If you are asking your subscribers to buy multiple products, sign up for another email list. Make sure to enable the action to be taken in as few clicks as possible.</li></ul><h3><strong>Forgetting to personalize campaigns</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>The best emails engage the audience. With people receiving dozens of promotional emails every day, tailoring them for the recipients helps you stand out in a crowded inbox. If every email tries to sell your products, your customers are going to become disengaged. </li>
<li>The best way forward is to segment your customer base. The tone of your subject line must resonate with your recipients.&nbsp;Make the recipients feel valued and make it their need to open the mail and take the desired action. It can be as simple as including a recipient’s name in the subject line like a personalised greeting.</li>
</ul><h3><strong>Not Brainstorming</strong></h3><ul><li>Personally speaking, i hate being too formal and professional. Many industries have shed their practice of being too formal. It might work on the military set up, but not on the creativity front. </li><li><a href="https://www.tidio.com/blog/abandoned-cart-email-subject-lines-examples/">47% of email recipients open email based on the subject line</a> alone. So be creative wherever possible. Write short subject lines that are clear and engaging. You can use emojis and use Bold fonts to make it appear interesting to click and open. Make sure to optimise for mobile and tablets to see if the font is big enough, the graphics or video looks good.</li></ul><h3><strong>Wrong timings</strong></h3><ul><li> Timing is an important aspect of email campaigns. <a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/sales/best-time-send-email-report-2015?&amp;_ga=2.141218610.1693432634.1531769354-1791073514.1499368195#sm.001o6d3zv162ceoascb2o9l50lh3z">Data from HubSpot</a> suggests that emails sent at 11 a.m. had the highest open rates. <a style="text-align: var(--text-align); letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://www.campaignmonitor.com/resources/guides/email-marketing-benchmarks/">Campaign Monitor</a> suggests that Wednesdays and Fridays are the best days to send emails. So sending emails at odd hours or days will get you lost in a crowded inbox. This will reduce open rates and obviously affecting your web traffic conversion rates.</li><li>Try experimenting with different times to see which time best engages your audience. For example, <a style="text-align: var(--text-align); letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://www.morningbrew.com/">Morning Brew</a> sends a daily email between 5 or 6 AM that details the latest happenings in the business world. The entire idea is that the news arrive early before the regular newspaper</li></ul><h3><strong>Neglecting analytics</strong></h3><ul><li>Once in a lifetime, it is better to look back. Emails are not sacrosanct, mistakes can and will happen. So consistently make sure to use analytics to verify that your efforts lead to something. Check the click-through rates, open rate of your email campaigns. So keeping an eye on how many new subscribers you are gaining and how many people unsubscribe is always the best approach.</li><li>Figure out your emails with the highest open and click-through rates and use that information when crafting future campaigns. </li></ul>		
			<h2>Overview</h2>		
		<p>Marketing is all about relationship. So make it a relationship worth fighting for. You can do it by effective communication and making the customer feel valued. For this, there is no other tool than Email Marketing. Standing out in a crowded inbox is not as hard as you imagine. Send yourself a test copy of your email and ask yourself if you would open the mail if you were the recipient. Otherwise, you’re just crowding their inbox. </p><p>By taking note of the above mentioned Email Marketing Mistakes, you can effectively make your Email marketing more engaging and converting, You can bolster your position as an industry expert while also gaining the trust of and building a relationship with customers. This will lead to higher open rates and improved conversion rates.</p>',
    'image' => 'assets/placeholders/blog-digital-marketing.svg',
    'published_at' => '2023-08-25 04:51:31',
    'active' => 1,
  ],
  [
    'id' => 42918,
    'slug' => 'essential-digital-marketing-strategies-for-small-businesses',
    'title' => 'Essential Digital Marketing Strategies for Small Businesses',
    'category' => 'Digital Marketing',
    'tags' => 'Digital Marketing',
    'author' => 'TechBound Team',
    'author_designation' => 'Digital Marketing Team',
    'excerpt' => 'The modern business landscape is a digital canvas painted with innovation and opportunity. In this realm, small businesses wield powerful tools that extend far beyond physical...',
    'body' => 'The modern business landscape is a digital canvas painted with innovation and opportunity. In this realm, small businesses wield powerful tools that extend far beyond physical storefronts. These tools are the digital marketing strategies, each one a key that unlocks doors to growth and success. Imagine these strategies as the threads that weave the tapestry of digital triumph: SEO\'s guidance, content\'s storytelling, social media\'s connectivity, Google\'s spotlight, email\'s intimacy, influencers\' impact, videos\' visual allure, and PPC advertising\'s precision. Join us on a journey through these Digital Marketing Strategies for Small Businesses to lead towards the pinnacles of success.
<h2>Search Engine Optimization (SEO)</h2>
Search engine optimization (SEO) is the foundation of any <a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/hubspot-blog-marketing-industry-trends-report?hubs_content=blog.hubspot.com%252Fmarketing%252Fsmall-business-marketing-guide&amp;hubs_content-cta=null&amp;hubs_post-cta=blognavcard-marketing">successful digital marketing campaign</a>. A robust SEO strategy ensures that your business\'s website ranks prominently on search engine results pages (SERPs). But how can this be achieved?
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">&nbsp;Keyword Planning: Think of keywords as the guiding stars in this digital odyssey. Identify relevant keywords that your target audience is likely to search for. Utilize keyword research tools to uncover high-traffic and low-competition keywords that align with your business offerings.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">On-Page Optimization: Consider your website a stage, and on-page optimization the spotlight that illuminates your content for search engines. Crafting alluring titles, meta descriptions, and headers that seamlessly integrate keywords is akin to setting the stage with the perfect lighting. This enhancement not only captivates search engine algorithms but also entices visitors to explore the rich content within.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Off-Page Strategies: In the digital world, establishing your domain extends beyond your virtual walls. Off-page strategies act as bridges connecting your brand with influential domains. Imagine them as ambassadors forging alliances with reputable sources. Building backlinks and guest posting on authoritative platforms becomes your virtual handshake, extending your influence and expanding your realm.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Content Marketing</h2>
Content marketing is a pivotal strategy that centers on providing value to your audience through informative and engaging content. Visualize content marketing as the key that opens the door to meaningful conversations. With each piece of content, whether a blog post, podcast, or infographic, businesses initiate a dialogue with their audience. Just as friends exchange stories around a campfire, businesses use content to create a virtual gathering place where ideas are shared, questions are answered, and connections are forged.
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Focus on Blogging: Regularly publish blog posts that address your audience\'s pain points, answer their questions, and offer solutions .By embarking on a blogging journey, you unlock a realm of possibility where your business becomes a guiding beacon for your audience. Dive into their world, addressing their pain points, answering their questions, and providing actionable solutions. As you share valuable insights, your business evolves into a trusted advisor, solidifying its reputation as an authoritative source in your industry. This establishes your business as an authoritative source in your industry.</li>
</ul>
<style>/*! elementor - v3.14.0 - 26-06-2023 */<br />
.elementor-widget-image{text-align:center}.elementor-widget-image a{display:inline-block}.elementor-widget-image a img[src$=".svg"]{width:48px}.elementor-widget-image img{vertical-align:middle;display:inline-block}</style>												<img width="1024" height="680" src="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Digital-Marketing-Strategies-for-Small-Businesses-1024x680.jpg" alt="Digital Marketing Strategies for Small Businesses" loading="lazy" srcset="https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Digital-Marketing-Strategies-for-Small-Businesses-1024x680.jpg 1024w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Digital-Marketing-Strategies-for-Small-Businesses-300x199.jpg 300w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Digital-Marketing-Strategies-for-Small-Businesses-768x510.jpg 768w, https://techbound.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Digital-Marketing-Strategies-for-Small-Businesses.jpg 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px">
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Frequency in Posting: Just as a familiar voice brings comfort, a steady stream of blog posts cultivates familiarity with your audience. Consistency is your secret ingredient, fostering engagement and anticipation. A well-maintained posting schedule is your commitment to be present, ensuring your audience always finds a reason to return for more knowledge, solutions, and inspiration.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Reliable Information: Ensure that your content is accurate, well-researched, and reliable. Every blog post is a testament to your dedication to accuracy and thorough research. By offering content that can be trusted, you build a bridge of credibility that spans beyond the screen, forging connections with your audience based on mutual respect.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Social Media Promotion: Share your blog posts across your social media platforms to broaden their reach and drive traffic back to your website. Through the magic of social media promotion, your content not only resonates with your existing audience but also finds its way to new shores. As your blog posts gather likes, shares, and comments, your business finds its place in the social discourse, where engagement flourishes.</li>
</ul>
<h2> Social Media Marketing</h2>
Social media has become an indispensable platform for brand building and customer engagement. It offers a direct line of communication between businesses and their target audience. As businesses harness its potential, they open a realm of engagement, empowerment, and interaction, transforming casual visitors into loyal advocates and turning digital landscapes into thriving communities.
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Brand Building: Leverage social media platforms to humanize your brand by sharing behind-the-scenes content, employee stories, and posts that reflect your brand\'s values. For instance, if your brand values sustainability, share content about eco-friendly practices you adopt or partnerships with environmental organizations. This helps your audience connect on a personal level, fostering loyalty and emotional resonance.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Visual Cohesion: Maintain a consistent visual identity across all social media platforms. Use the same color schemes, typography, and imagery in your posts, profile pictures, and banners. This coherence reinforces your brand\'s identity and makes it easier for followers to recognize your content instantly, leading to improved brand recall.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Offerings and Solutions: Showcasing your products or services on social media provides a dynamic platform to highlight their features and benefits. Create engaging posts, videos, and stories that demonstrate how your offerings can solve problems or enhance the lives of your target audience. This not only drives sales but also establishes your brand as a reliable solution provider.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Dedicated Social Media Management: Assign someone to manage your social media accounts exclusively. This ensures timely responses, content sharing, and engagement.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Social Media Advertising: Invest in paid social media advertising to expand your reach beyond your followers. Target specific demographics to reach potential customers.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Google Listing</h2>
In a world where local businesses are striving to stand out, Google My Business (GMB) emerges as the game-changing solution. Google My Business (GMB) is a powerful tool for local businesses to enhance their online visibility and improve customer engagement. Seamlessly integrating into the digital landscape, GMB empowers businesses to take control of their online presence. Through detailed business listings, eye-catching visuals, and real-time interactions, <a href="https://techbound.in/5-simple-hacks-to-top-google-business-profile/">GMB not only boosts visibility but also fosters meaningful connections with local customers.</a>
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Complete Profile: Create a comprehensive GMB profile with accurate business information, such as address, phone number, and business hours.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Ratings, Opinions, and Photos: Encourage customers to leave reviews on your GMB listing. Positive reviews build credibility, while photos showcase your products or services.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Email Marketing</h2>
Email marketing remains an effective way to nurture leads and strengthen relationships with your audience.

Seamlessly bridging the gap between your brand and your audience, email marketing is a proven method to nurture leads and cultivate lasting relationships. With its personalized approach and targeted messaging, it\'s a dynamic tool that delivers results.&nbsp;
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Relationship Building: Creating a well-structured email marketing campaign that guides leads through a journey of getting to know your brand, its values, and offerings.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Influencer Marketing</h2>
Breaking away from the ordinary, your brand\'s ascent to greater heights is within reach through strategic influencer partnerships. Collaborating with influencers who have a substantial following in your industry can amplify your brand\'s reach.
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Industry Relevance: Partner with influencers whose values align with your brand. Their endorsement can introduce your business to a wider audience.</li>
</ul>
<h2> Video Marketing</h2>
In a world where attention spans are fleeting, video content stands as the beacon of captivating communication. Video content is highly engaging and can communicate complex ideas in a dynamic manner.
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Audience Connection: Use videos to showcase products, share behind-the-scenes glimpses, and provide tutorials or how-to guides. Venture into the world of visual storytelling and witness how the magic of video can reshape the way you convey, captivate, and leave a lasting impact.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pay-Per-Click (PPC) Advertising</h2>
PPC advertising is a targeted approach to driving immediate traffic and generating leads.

By positioning your brand precisely where it matters, you\'re not just sparking attention, but sparking conversions.
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Keyword Research: Thoroughly research keywords relevant to your business and industry. This ensures your ads are shown to the right audience.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Compelling Ad Copy: Craft persuasive ad copy that entices users to click through to your website. Highlight your unique value proposition.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Understanding Your Target Audience</h2>
Understanding your target audience\'s preferences, pain points, and behaviors is essential for crafting effective marketing campaigns. The key to unlocking success lies in understanding your audience at a profound level. By unraveling the threads of their preferences, pain points, and behaviors, you gain the insights needed to craft campaigns that truly resonate. This strategic approach not only connects your brand with its intended recipients but also lays the foundation for impactful and memorable marketing endeavors.
<h2>Encourage Customer Reviews</h2>
Positive online reviews serve as social proof and can influence potential customers. Embrace the potential of customer reviews as a dynamic tool that not only reflects satisfaction but shapes it. From validating choices to fostering a sense of belonging, the influence of positive online reviews is unparalleled.
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<a href="https://techbound.in/how-to-promote-your-small-medium-business-on-google/">Digital marketing is a cornerstone for small businesses aiming to expand their reach and build lasting relationships with their audience.</a> By embracing a well-rounded approach, these businesses can connect with their audience and expand their horizons. With digital marketing as their compass, small businesses can navigate the complexities of the online world and chart a course towards success.',
