Record Keeping -Do they have a good record-keeping system?
<h2>What is the responsibility of a marketing agency?</h2>
An advertising agency is an organization that creates and executes campaign ideas, which can range from cross-promotion to brand awareness to product placement. They specialize in one or more specific industries and can operate internationally. Advertising agencies typically do:
<ol>
 	<li> Conduct research on the market, including consumer demographics and preferences, to design relevant types of advertising campaigns.</li>
 	<li> Create advertising campaigns that target a particular audience or demographic with a specific message or concept.</li>
 	<li> Gather data to report back to clients on the effectiveness of their advertising (i.e., through media buys and performance tracking).</li>
 	<li> Do advertising campaigns to ensure they are executed according to plan.</li>
 	<li> Create and produce marketing materials, such as press releases, online advertisements, infographics, videos/films/TV commercials, PowerPoint presentations, and ads for social media sites like Facebook or Twitter.</li>
 	<li> Monitor the performance of marketing campaigns by tracking audience engagement through various digital channels (i.e., social media, online content, etc.).</li>
</ol>
<h2>Conclusion: Our Three Steps To Hiring A Result Driven Digital Marketing Agency</h2>
There are a lot of digital marketing agencies out there, and it cannot be easy to find the one that best suits your needs. It\'s important to take time and research before deciding.
<ul>
 	<li>The first step is finding an agency with the skills you need.</li>
 	<li>This includes reviewing past work, reading reviews, and talking to current or former clients.</li>
 	<li>The second step is checking their portfolio for the services they offer. And finally, the third step is checking their pricing structure and contract terms, so you know what you\'re getting into before signing anything.</li>
</ul>',
