<h2>Digital marketing Interview Questions for Specialists and Managers</h2>
<h4><b>How do On-Page SEO and Off-Page SEO differ from one another?</b></h4>
By making substantial changes to web pages, on-page SEO techniques increase website traffic. On-Page Optimization includes tasks like increasing page load speed, website structure, the title tag, internal linking, meta tags, writing quality content, etc.&nbsp;

Off-page SEO refers to activities that increase your website\'s visibility, trustworthiness, domain authority, etc. but also on search engines. Off-page activities include building relevant backlinks, marketing on social media, and writing guest posts for blogs, Quora, etc.&nbsp;&nbsp;
<h4><b>What methodology would you use for keyword research?&nbsp;</b></h4>
Any SEO specialist\'s primary responsibility is to do this, so this inquiry is inevitable. The following advice should be kept in mind as you answer because it requires a very strong understanding of keyword analysis:&nbsp;
<ul>
 	<li><strong>Mention the search volume tool you\'d employ to identify the best keywords. </strong></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 	<li><strong>According to their relevance and level of competition, chose keywords.&nbsp;</strong></li>
</ul>
<h4><b>What are the most popular SEO tools?</b>&nbsp;</h4>
While performing SEO, a variety of tools are available. Here are a few well-known and frequently used tools, both paid and unpaid: Keywords Everywhere, Ubersuggest, Seomofo, SEO Review Tools, Search Console, Google Trends, <a href="https://www.semrush.com/">SEMRush</a>, Ahrefs, and Moz are examples of SEO tools.
<h4><b>How would your SEO strategy for improving our website\'s functionality look?&nbsp;</b></h4>
When outlining your plan, be concise and clear. Again, if you\'re worried that they\'ll use your methods without hiring you, just give a quick summary. Be confident in your plan\'s presentation and use statistics to support your assertions.&nbsp;
<h4><b>Briefly describe Google AdWords.</b></h4>
Google AdWords is a pay-per-click (PPC) online advertising platform designed to give marketers a way to run their ads in front of potentially targeted audiences. Google AdWords offers advertisers two channels to reach people, in contrast to other pay-per-click platforms like Facebook Ads:&nbsp;
