 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Develop your skills</b>: Digital marketing requires a variety of skills, including content creation, social media marketing, SEO, and data analysis. Work on practical projects or finish online courses to hone your skills in advance.&nbsp;</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Prepare to share your experience</b>: Be prepared to share your experiences using particular tools and platforms as well as examples of past campaigns or projects that you have worked on.&nbsp;</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Display your creativity</b>: Since digital marketing requires it, be ready to demonstrate your talent for it and come up with fresh campaign concepts during the interview.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Prove your analytical prowess by discussing how you\'ve used data to improve campaigns and get results. Digital marketing also involves analyzing and interpreting data.</li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1">Finally, demonstrate your enthusiasm and passion for the business and the sector. Being open to learning and adapting is crucial because the field of digital marketing is constantly changing.</li>
</ul>',
