    'slug' => 'how-to-optimize-blog-for-high-ranking',
    'title' => 'How to Optimize Your Blog for High Ranking',
    'category' => 'Search Engine Optimization',
    'tags' => 'Search Engine Optimization',
    'author' => 'TechBound Team',
    'author_designation' => 'Digital Marketing Team',
    'excerpt' => 'The blogging landscape is constantly evolving, and to stay ahead, you need to adapt . Here\'s what your blog needs to thrive in 2024: The Anatomy of a Perfect Blog For Higher...',
    'body' => 'The blogging landscape is constantly evolving, and <a href="https://copyblogger.com/content-marketing/">to stay ahead, you need to adapt</a>. Here\'s what your blog needs to thrive in 2024:
<h2><b>The Anatomy of a Perfect Blog For Higher Ranking</b></h2>
<h3><strong>1. SEO Meta Data</strong></h3>
<h5><strong>Title: Captivating, keyword-rich, under 60 characters.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Meta Description: Compelling summary, enticing clicks, around 150 characters.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>URL: Short, descriptive, includes target keyword.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Schema Markup: Helps search engines understand your content better.</strong></h5>
<h3><strong>2. Engaging Headline &amp; Heading Structure</strong></h3>
<h5><strong>Headline: Grabs attention, promises value.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Heading Structure (H2, H3, etc.): Organises content, makes it scannable.</strong></h5>
<h3><strong>3. Compelling Content:</strong></h3>
<h5><strong>Length: 700+ words is a good starting point for SEO.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Original Images: Visually appealing, relevant to the topic.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Alt Attributes: Describe images for accessibility and SEO.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Table of Contents: Improves user experience, especially for longer posts.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Internal Links: Guide readers to other relevant content on your site.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Rich Media: Embed videos, podcasts, or interactive elements.</strong></h5>
<h5><strong>Call to Action (CTA): Prompt readers to subscribe, comment, or share.</strong></h5>
